#: vncviewer/org.tigervnc.vncviewer.metainfo.xml.in:13
#: vncviewer/vncviewer.desktop.in.in:2
msgid "TigerVNC"
msgstr "TigerVNC"

#: vncviewer/org.tigervnc.vncviewer.metainfo.xml.in:14
#: vncviewer/vncviewer.desktop.in.in:4
msgid "Connect to VNC server and display remote desktop"
msgstr "Savienoties ar VNC serveri un rādīt attālo darbvirsmu"

#: vncviewer/org.tigervnc.vncviewer.metainfo.xml.in:17
msgid "Virtual Network Computing (VNC) is a remote display system that allows you to view and interact with a virtual desktop environment running on another computer on the network. Using VNC, you can run graphical applications on a remote machine and send only the display from these applications to your local device. This package contains a client which will enable you to connect to other desktops running a VNC server. VNC is platform-independent and supports various operating systems and architectures as both servers and clients."
msgstr "Virtual Network Computing (VNC) ir attālās attēlošanas sistēma, kas ļauj skatīt virtuālu darbvirsmas vidi, kas darbojas citā tīkla datorā, un mijiedarboties ar to. Izmantojot VNC, varat palaist grafiskas lietotnes attālā datorā un uz savu lokālo ierīci sūtīt tikai šo lietotņu attēlu. Šajā pakotnē ir klients, kas ļauj savienoties ar citām darbvirsmām, kurās darbojas VNC serveris. VNC ir neatkarīgs no platformas un atbalsta dažādas operētājsistēmas un arhitektūras gan kā serveri, gan kā klienti."

#: vncviewer/org.tigervnc.vncviewer.metainfo.xml.in:23
msgid "TigerVNC is a high-speed version of VNC based on the RealVNC 4 and X.org code bases. TigerVNC started as a next-generation development effort for TightVNC on Unix and Linux platforms, but it split from its parent project in early 2009 so that TightVNC could focus on Windows platforms. TigerVNC supports a variant of Tight encoding that is greatly accelerated by the use of the libjpeg-turbo JPEG codec."
msgstr "TigerVNC ir ātrdarbīga VNC versija, kuras pamatā ir RealVNC 4 un X.org koda bāzes. TigerVNC sākās kā nākamās paaudzes TightVNC izstrādes projekts Unix un Linux platformām, taču 2009. gada sākumā tas atdalījās no sava sākotnējā projekta, lai TightVNC varētu koncentrēties uz Windows platformām. TigerVNC atbalsta Tight kodējuma variantu, kas ir ievērojami paātrināts, izmantojot JPEG kodeku libjpeg-turbo."

